# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  OutLead — environment configuration
#
#  Copy this file to `.env` and fill it in:      cp .env.example .env
#
#  `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit real credentials, and never paste them
#  into an issue, a screenshot, or a chat. If a key leaks, rotate it.
#
#  Nothing here is required to try the scraper. Each section unlocks one more
#  stage of the pipeline, and every stage degrades gracefully when its keys
#  are missing — the system tells you what's off instead of failing silently.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. SENDING (required to send any email at all) ────────────────────────
#
# Gmail needs an "App Password", NOT your normal password:
#   1. Turn on 2-Step Verification on the Google account
#   2. Create one at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords
#   3. Paste the 16-character value below (spaces are fine)
#
# Any SMTP provider works — change the host/port in config.py's SMTP block.
# Use a SEPARATE sending address, never your main inbox: cold outreach can
# damage a domain's reputation, and you don't want that on your primary.
SMTP_EMAIL=you@yourdomain.com
SMTP_APP_PASSWORD=xxxx xxxx xxxx xxxx

# The ONLY address the "Send test email" button can ever reach. Put your own
# inbox here so you can see exactly what a lead receives before going live.
# Defaults to SMTP_EMAIL if unset. It is never influenced by request data,
# so no click (or crafted request) can aim a test at a real lead.
TEST_SEND_ADDRESS=you@yourdomain.com


# ── 2. YOUR IDENTITY (required before live sending — see note) ────────────
#
# This appears in every email's footer. An honest sender identity and a
# working opt-out are the baseline for CAN-SPAM / PECR compliance.
#
# LIVE SENDING IS BLOCKED while these are still the shipped placeholders, so
# a fresh clone can never email strangers signed "Your Name" with someone
# else's booking link. Set them before you flip the send gate.
OUTREACH_FROM_NAME=Your Name
OUTREACH_TITLE=Founder
OUTREACH_BUSINESS_NAME=Your Company
OUTREACH_WEBSITE=yourcompany.com

# Where you want replies to land. Any scheduling link works (Calendly, Cal.com,
# SavvyCal, TidyCal). This is the ONLY link the AI is allowed to put in an
# email — it writes the placeholder [BOOK_LINK] and the renderer substitutes
# this URL, so the model can never invent a different one.
OUTREACH_BOOKING_URL=https://cal.com/your-handle/intro-call

# The opt-out line in every footer. Keep it human, keep it honest, and keep
# the word UNSUBSCRIBE — the reply checker watches for it and suppresses that
# address permanently.
OUTREACH_REPLY_NOTE=Not a fit? Just reply UNSUBSCRIBE and I'll show myself out for good — no hard feelings.


# ── 3. WHAT YOU SELL (drives every email the AI writes) ───────────────────
#
# This is the ONLY description of your offer in the whole system. The model
# writes all three emails from it, so be concrete and specific. Two plain
# sentences beat a paragraph of marketing language.
OUTREACH_WHAT_YOU_SELL=an AI phone assistant for local businesses: it answers every call 24/7 like a friendly human, books appointments straight into their calendar, and follows up with people who didn't book.

# The pain you lead with — the reason a stranger should keep reading past
# line one. Write it as the problem THEY have, not the feature you built.
OUTREACH_ANGLE=they lose customers every time a call goes unanswered, after hours or while the team is busy, and those callers just ring the next business on the list.


# ── 4. AI EMAIL WRITING (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Without this key the pipeline still scrapes, enriches, verifies and
# qualifies — leads simply have no emails written yet, and the sender skips
# them loudly rather than sending anything unreviewed.
#
# Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Cost is tiny: a full 3-email sequence per lead is ~$0.001 on gpt-4o-mini
# (about 4 cents for 40 leads). A hard spending cap lives in config.py's
# LLM["budget_usd"] and stops the writer dead once reached.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-your-key-here


# ── 5. MAILBOX VERIFICATION (optional, strongly recommended) ──────────────
#
# MX records only prove a DOMAIN accepts mail — not that the mailbox exists.
# Bounces are the fastest way to wreck a new sending reputation, so this
# checks each inbox for real before a lead is ever queued.
#
# Free tier with recurring credits: https://emailverifier.reoon.com
# Without it, verification falls back to syntax + MX + placeholder rules.
REOON_API_KEY=your-reoon-key-here
